Kubernetes Architecture Overview

It has two components:
	Control plane
	Data Plane
Control plane consists:
	Kube API Server
	etcd
	scheduler
	controller manager
Data plane consists
	Kubelet
	Kubeproxy
	runc

	

What is Control Plane?
The control plane is the brain of the Kubernetes cluster
Making decisions about the cluster
Maintaining desired state
Scheduling workloads
Managing cluster wide configuration
Responding to failures
Control plane = Decision maker

What is Data Plane?
The Data Plane consists of worker nodes
Running application containers
Executing instructions given by the control plane
Reporting node and pod status
Data Plane = Execution engine

Control Plane components:

Kube-apiserver:
	ApiGateway -> authenticate and authorize
( Linux : Everything is FILE, K8S: Everything is API)
	Entry point of the cluster
	Accepts REST API requests
	Validates requests
	Stores cluster state in etcd
	Servers as communication hub
	Everything in Kubernetes talks to the API Server

etcd:
	Distributed Key-value store
	Stores entired cluster state
	POD/Deployment/Services info
	etcd is the single source of truth
	If etcd is lost without backup, cluster state is lost

Kube-Scheduler:
	Assign pods to nodes
	Makes placement decisions

Controller Manager
	Multiple types of controller manager
	Controller manager watches the cluster current state and tries to match with desired state


Data Plane Components:
Kubelet
	Agent running on each node
	Talks to API Server
	Receives pod specifications from KubeAPI Server
	
Container RUntime - ContainerD -> Who actually launches the container
Kubeproxy 
	Handles network routing
	Manages iptables or IPVS rules
	Implements Services



