$ minikube start --driver=docker


$ kubectl get nodes
$ kubectl get pods
$ kubectl get ns
$ kubectl get pof -n kube-system



K8S is an orchestration tool
The main purpose is not to just run the container/pod
The main function is to maintain the desired state of application
watch-> act-> reconcile

Application -> Container -> Pod -> Inside the K8S cluster

What is Desired state/Requirements:
	How many pods should run
	Which container image to use
	What port to expose
	How many replicas should exist
	.......

How to pass my desire state to K8S
	Imperative way : Step by step what to do directly at console using kubectl
			 No documentation, No VCS
	Declarative way : We write an yaml file which is called manifest
			kubectl apply -f <>
			Creates objects and k8s keep monitoring the objects




